# Test Patterns for Novelwriter Integration Tests

## Test file structure
Follow test_character_integration_chain.py and test_plotting_subagent.py
as the canonical patterns. Every test file must have:

1. @pytest.fixture(autouse=True) setup_test_db that:
   - Sets MONGODB_DB_NAME to "novelwriter_test_kg"
   - Calls init_kg_db("novelwriter_test_kg")
   - Deletes all nodes and edges before the test
   - Seeds the specific nodes required for this skill
   - Yields (cleanup runs on exit)

2. @pytest.mark.integration on every test function

3. Run command in docstring:
   uv run pytest <filename> -s -v -m integration

---

## KG fixture requirements by skill

### scene-construction
Requires Character node with FULL voice_profile sub-record in properties.
Minimum voice_profile structure (all five dimensions required):
{
  "vocabulary_range": {
    "lexical_register": "informal, direct",
    "signature_vocabulary_categories": ["spatial", "threat assessment"],
    "avoids": ["courtly register"]
  },
  "sentence_structure_patterns": {
    "default_sentence_length": "short and declarative",
    "structural_habits": "observation before interpretation",
    "under_stress": "fragments, no subordination"
  },
  "observational_focus": {
    "primary_lens": "exits and physical threats",
    "secondary_lens": "who holds leverage",
    "systematic_blind_spots": "emotional need in others",
    "how_they_read_people": "hands and feet before faces"
  },
  "internal_thought_patterns": {
    "deliberative_style": "instinct-first",
    "self_monitoring": "minimal",
    "memory_intrusion": "sensory triggers only",
    "relationship_to_time": "present-focused"
  },
  "emotional_processing_style": {
    "speed_of_acknowledgment": "slow",
    "internal_expression": "displaced onto physical observation",
    "what_they_cannot_look_at": "own complicity in past failures",
    "under_extreme_pressure": "affect flattens"
  }
}

Also seed: KnowledgeItem node + KNOWS edge for the character.
Also seed: Location node for the scene setting.

### pov-consistency-maintenance
Do NOT chain from scene-construction output. Use a hardcoded draft.
The hardcoded draft MUST contain at least one deliberate violation so
VIOLATIONS FOUND is the expected result and violation_log can be verified.

Standard violation to embed (head-hop):
DRAFT_WITH_VIOLATION = (
    "Elara pressed herself against the cold stone wall. "
    "The guards were two corridors away — she could hear their boots. "
    "She needed the eastern passage. "
    "Kael, waiting outside, felt a surge of anxiety as he wondered "
    "if she had been caught. "
    "She moved toward the drain cover and pulled it open."
)
Expected: overall_status == "VIOLATIONS FOUND"
Expected: violation_log contains entry with violation_type == "Head-Hopping"

### consequence-cascade-implementation
Requires TWO Character nodes + ONE RELATIONSHIP edge between them.
The consequence must propagate across the relationship to be meaningful.
Also seed: an existing CascadeChain node to test the extend_existing path.

### gardener-plotting-system (already tested — do not modify)
Pattern in test_plotting_subagent.py is the reference.

